  "Hi, I am Mike Hall. Today I am revisiting the conversation with Ginny Hendry. Here is what brought me back to it.",
  "This conversation was recorded at WindyCityRails 2012 (2012) in 2012. Ginny Hendry was the quiet, generous heart of ChicagoRuby and 8th Light. Transitioning from decades of Fortran and systems engineering into Ruby, she organized and taught Chicago RailsBridge workshops and launched hands-on hack nights downtown, leaving an enduring legacy of learning after her 2017 passing.",
  "The question I want to follow is: What does it take to make a room full of strangers feel like a community where you belong? How do we build technical spaces that welcome those who have never seen a terminal?",
  "Let us watch the original conversation. I will pause where I want to look more closely.",
  "Here is what stood out to me. I will show the source and explain what I think it supports.",
  "That is what I took from this conversation. The recording and transcript are linked from just3ws.com."
